# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Added during the 2026-11-13 cleanup, before this repository's first commit.
# A dry run of `git add -A` against the rules above would have committed 145 MB
# of packaging output. Every pattern below sits on its own line: in .gitignore a
# "#" only starts a comment at the beginning of a line, so a trailing inline
# comment becomes part of the pattern and the rule then matches nothing at all.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# build/ is NOT ignored wholesale, and that distinction is load-bearing.
# build/app.ico and build/version_info.txt are authored inputs: "SKEER MIDI
# VAULT.spec" passes them as icon= and version=, and
# packaging/build_installer.ps1 reads both from build\. Ignoring build/ would
# silently drop them and break packaging from a clean checkout.
# build/work/ was already covered above. build/tools/ is a vendored Inno Setup
# install (28 MB) that was placed here by hand: packaging/build_installer.ps1
# looks for ISCC.exe in several known locations and fails the preflight when none
# of them has it, so a clean checkout needs Inno Setup installed or INNO_SETUP_ISCC
# set. Nothing in the pipeline downloads it.
build/tools/

# Regenerated from build_installer.ps1's CLI flags on every run (--specpath
# build). The authored spec is the tracked one at the repo root.
build/SKEER MIDI VAULT.spec

# Written by scripts/build_stamp.py and read back out of the bundle as
# _internal\buildinfo\BUILDINFO.json. It records the commit and tree digests of
# the checkout that produced a build, so it belongs to that build, not to the
# source: a tracked copy would claim to be provenance for bytes it never stamped.
build/BUILDINFO.json

# Unified deliverables folder: standalone bundle, Setup exe, portable ZIP and
# SHA256SUMS.txt. Regenerate with packaging/build_installer.ps1. Nothing inside
# launch/ is tracked, in this or any other SKEER project.
launch/

# Superseded by launch/. Still ignored so pre-existing copies do not reappear
# in git status.
dist/
dist-installer/

# web/dist/ stays ignored, which is this project's convention and the opposite
# of what dj-library and sample-vault do. packaging/build_installer.ps1 runs
# `npm run build` but never `npm ci`, so a checkout with no web/node_modules
# needs that once first. start.ps1 handles both automatically.

# The VST3 form lives in plugin/. This is the CMake tree, and unlike build/ at
# the repo root there is nothing authored inside it: every byte is output of
# `plugin/build.ps1`, including a whole JUCE build and the built .vst3 bundle.
plugin/build/
